From 48617068fcd8892aab048d1103f5291415981e89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:13:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] release: every port from one dispatch, and a CI job for the
 version gate

release.yml releases every port at VERSION in one run. tools/release_plan.py
decides what each port still needs: typescript and javascript publish to npm,
go is a tag alone, and a port already released at VERSION is skipped only
while its directory is unchanged since its tag. Every tag goes up in one
atomic push, after every publish has succeeded and the go module has built
and passed its tests with no workspace, as a consumer resolves it. A pushed
go/v* tag starts a run too, and any pushed tag must be one of VERSION's.

The security shape is unchanged: plan, npm and go hold contents: read, the
publish job alone holds id-token: write and checks nothing out, and the tag
job runs git alone.

build.yml gains a `versions` job for `make version-check` and the release
plan's tests, so the gate no longer rides on vendor-check and pack-diff.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
